From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:38:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 154/159] arm64: dts: qcom: nairo: Enable WLED CABC

Make the WLED follow the panel's content-adaptive backlight signal, as
downstream does, except below brightness 200 where downstream switches
it off (mmi,low-bl-threshold).

This patch was generated by an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5 in
Claude Code) during an interactive bring-up session on a Motorola Moto G
5G Plus (XT2075-3, "nairo"). It has not yet been reviewed line by line
by a human and needs that review before any submission.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts
index eeaba233d9a7..78b23ac7e399 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts
@@ -536,6 +536,13 @@ &pm8150l_wled {
 	qcom,current-limit-microamp = <25000>;
 	qcom,ovp-millivolt = <20500>;
 	qcom,num-strings = <4>;
+	/*
+	 * Follow the panel's content-adaptive backlight (CABC) signal, as
+	 * downstream does, except below brightness 200 where downstream
+	 * switches it off (mmi,low-bl-threshold).
+	 */
+	qcom,cabc-sel = <1>;
+	qcom,cabc-min-brightness = <200>;
 
 	status = "okay";
 };
